    "https://www2.aston.ac.uk/staff-public/hr/jobs": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Jobs at Aston | Aston University We use cookies to enhance your online experience Our website uses cookies to distinguish you from other users of our website. This enables the University to provide you with a good experience when you browse our website and also allows us to take steps to improve our website. By continuing to browse the site, you are agreeing to our use of cookies. Required For the session cookies, EU cookie pop up cookies, etc. Analytics For the Google Analytics and Crazy Egg cookies Marketing For the Facebook pixel cookies Save preferences Reject all Accept all categories Update preferences Skip to main content Study locations: Birmingham | London | Online Find a course Search Menu Header top menu About International students Clearing for international students Applying to Aston Scholarships International Partnerships Aston students Student Portal (OneAston) New students Alumni Staff Search Main navigation Clearing Clearing 2026 Clearing vacancies Clearing Guide Your career Courses A to Z of Courses Clearing 2026 Undergraduate Open Days Open Days, events and webinars Why choose Aston? Study at Aston Teaching and learning Undergraduate Postgraduate Postgraduate research International students Foundation Programmes Degree apprenticeships Online courses Work-based degrees Student life Welcome Week Virtual tour Fees and Finance Accommodation Student support Student Union Careers and Placements Library and Learning Services Student life at Aston Birmingham life Commuting to university Research Research at Aston Research Excellence Framework Impact case studies Supporting our researchers Knowledge Exchange Research and Enterprise department Research degrees Find Experts For Business Talent Expertise Space Aston Business Hub Find a course About International students Clearing for international students Applying to Aston Scholarships International Partnerships Aston students Student Portal (OneAston) New students Alumni Staff X Find your course Search View your bookmarked courses Advanced filters Course level Foundation programmes Undergraduate degrees Degree apprenticeships Postgraduate MA/MSc courses MBA Professional courses/CPD Work-based learning Research degrees/PhD DBA Online courses Courses by subject Audiology Biosciences Business Computer Science Cybersecurity Economics Engineering and Physical Sciences English Language and Literature History Law Mathematics Medicine Neuroscience Nursing Optometry Pharmacy Politics and International Relations Psychology Sociology and Criminology Course type Full-time Full-time (Hons) Full-time / Part-time Full-time or part-time (Hons) Online/distance learning (Hons) Part-time (Hons) Part-time / distance learning Part-time - Blended Part-time, Online / distance learning Professional short courses/CPD Work-based degree (Hons) Part-time Online / distance learning Work-based degree Aston University London Course format Placement year (UK/abroad) Integrated placements Integrated placement year Integrated international placement Internship / overseas study Optional placement year Work-based learning Experiential learning No placements Beginner’s language routes Available through clearing - Any - True False Apply filters Clear all Home Staff Public Human Resources Jobs at Aston Clearing 2026: Apply now - view our vacancies Jobs at Aston View All Current Vacancies Apply today Find out more View Academic Vacancies Apply today Find out more Benefits and Rewards Together we'll shape the future Find out more You'll never stop moving Thank you for considering Aston University. We think we have a lot to offer positive, team-spirited, ambitious people like you. We’re much more than a thriving Higher Education institution; we’re a world-class organisation using research and teaching to bring positive change to business, commerce and government, while opening up professional careers to talented students, regardless of background. We’re right at the heart of Birmingham, one of Europe’s liveliest and most welcoming cities, on a friendly and green 40-acre campus with excellent facilities. Working at Aston University, you’ll enjoy a competitive salary, great benefits and fantastic development opportunities. Over 1,900 formally contracted people work at the University in a wide variety of professional, technical, academic, manual and clerical roles. We recruit to fill vacancies as they arise so please check our website regularly for the most recent opportunities. You can find the latest opportunities by clicking on View Current Vacancies link on this page. Find out more Working at Aston ㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤ About us ㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤ Overseas Candidates ㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤ Birmingham ㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤㅤ Diversity and Inclusion Developing an inclusive workplace Find out more Social Impact Our impact in the region Find out more Aston Strategy Read more about Aston 2030 Strategy Find out more How to apply for a vacancy Once you've found a role that matches your skills and experience, click the Apply Online button. You’ll be asked to register and set up an account or log into your existing account if you've already created one. The online application screens are designed to collect the information that is required from you in a clear and structured way. Please ensure that you complete all of the fields. Help will be available to guide you through the form. You can complete your application in stages and you can login/logout at any time. You will be able to save and edit your application at any point BEFORE submission. Only when you have submitted your completed application will our recruiting managers be able to see it. Please note that CVs will only be accepted if accompanied by a completed application form. The system enables you to upload your CV. However this should be in addition to – not instead of – completing the online application screens.  To support our commitment to equality, diversity, and a fair recruitment process, Aston University will conduct anonymous shortlisting for certain roles. If this applies, it will be indicated in the job advertisement. For these roles, CVs will not be included in the shortlisting process. The job details and university information are written to provide you with a clear understanding of the role and skills, knowledge and experience you need to fill it. Please use these as the main points of reference when completing the application screens. In the final section, please write a statement to support your application. Think about any relevant skills and experience you’ve not already referred to.  These don’t have to be from current or previous roles; they can be taken from non-work related activities. The email address you provide in your application should be one you use regularly, because that’s how we’ll keep in touch with you throughout the process. All online applications must be received by midnight on the closing date. The day after submission, you’ll receive an acknowledgement email. Once you have submitted your application, you can view it at any time, along with the job details and university information. Just log into your account and visit the 'My Applications' area. You will not be able to amend your application once you have submitted it. If you do not have access to the internet to complete your application online, please contact the recruitment team on recruitment@aston.ac.uk . If you know the reference number for the job you’re interested in, please also quote this in your email. We will send you a paper application form. These must be received before midday on the closing date. Once the selection panel have assessed all applicants, we’ll get in touch, by email, to let you know the outcome. Please email recruitment@aston.ac.uk if you need further assistance, and the best of luck. Recruitment Standards - Guidance for Applicants Please find attached the Recruitment Standards which outline Aston University's commitment to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our students, staff, and visitors. They provide a framework for conducting thorough employment checks on all prospective employees. This document serves to inform applicants about the standards expected during the recruitment process. Document recruitment-standards-guidance-for-applicants.pdf 154.9 KB Frequently Asked Questions Application FAQs Technical FAQs What happens if the role I am applying for requires a DBS check? As part of our employee recruitment processes, Aston University use an umbrella body called First Advantage (FADV) Online Disclosures to process and interpret the results of DBS applications.  First Advantage provide a comprehensive DBS service with full UK coverage, including Disclosure Scotland DBS checking service. If your role requires a DBS check, HR will arrange for you to have access to an online application via a simple and easy-to-use online portal that links to the DBS.  We will communicate the results of your check through the online portal. This will then be stored electronically on your Core Employee Record for the period that the DBS is required.  The DBS certificate will be sent directly to your home address by DBS. Further details relating to GDPR and how your data is stored by First Advantage can be found here. What is the Disability Confident Scheme Aston University is a Disability Confident Committed Employer Level 2: Disability Confident Employer- GOV.UK.  If you have a disability and you meet the essential criteria for the role you applied for, you are guaranteed an interview. Employment of Ex-Offenders Our policy exists to ensure we treat all applicants who have a criminal record fairly and do not discriminate unfairly against candidates with either a spent or an unspent conviction. At the same time the policy is here to safeguard the University, our staff, students, visitors and service users.  The policy explains how we will seek information from you about past spent and unspent convictions, how this information will be used, and how we will deal with information relating to offences for posts exempted under the ROA. Policy on the Recruitment and Retention of Ex-Offenders Right to Work Checks Aston University is required to complete a Right to Work check for all workers and employees before they commence work. This check is usually completed digitally during the onboarding process. Occasionally, individuals may need to attend an in-person appointment with HR to provide their documents. It’s essential that your Right to Work check is completed before you start work at Aston. Contact our recruitment team if you have any questions about your check. Visas and Immigration Aston University is an ‘A’ rated sponsor. As a result, we are able to sponsor individuals to come and work at the University. We are only able to sponsor employees and roles that meet the criteria laid down by UK Visas and Immigration. If you are interested in a role at Aston, but require Sponsorship to obtain a work visa, please visit the UKVI’s website for the up to date criteria: UK Visas and Immigration (UKVI) Homepage You can also view immigration information for applicants/potential employees here. Queries? Please contact our recruitment team. Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn Youtube TSR Wechat #TeamAston Schools Aston Business School Aston Doctoral School Aston Medical School Aston Pharmacy School School of Computer Science and Digital Technologies School of Engineering and Innovation School of Law and Social Sciences School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences School of Psychology, Health and Clinical Sciences Aston University Engineering Academy and Sixth Form Aston University Goldsmiths Institute Aston University Mathematics School More Information Student support services News Press office Open days Jobs and vacancies Aston Global Aston Online Report and Support Preventing and responding to harassment and sexual misconduct Freedom of speech Student Recruitment and Outreach Contact Us Aston University Birmingham B4 7ET UK +44 (0)121 204 3000 Visit us University departments Please ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of website accessibility © Aston University Accessibility Cookies Disclaimer Publication Scheme Modern Slavery Act Privacy Back to top"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Terms": {
      "title": "Terms and Conditions",
      "description": "Terms and Conditions - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Terms and Conditions Your personal data will be processed in compliance with the DPA and from 25 May 2018 the GDPR The University’s Data Protection Policy and Privacy Notices, including the Job Applicant Privacy Notice can be found here http://www.aston.ac.uk/data-protection/ Access to the Aston University jobs website is restricted to staff of Aston University and applicants. To use the site you must agree to the Data Protection Statement and Terms of Use. Data Protection Statement Your data is securely held on a server at the University which has in place all the security measures required. Data you enter into the system will be treated confidentially and with respect. The data will not be disclosed to any external organisations except where an external body is party to the recruitment process. The application data will be removed twelve months after the vacancy is finished. Should you be successful in obtaining employment with Aston University, the University will use your personal data for the purpose of employee personnel administration and any legitimate issues relating to your employment with the University. In doing so, the University will observe at all times, the data protection principles embodied in the Data Protection Act 1998 and from 25 May 2018 with the GDPR Aston University will seek your explicit permission should it intend to process any sensitive personal data for any reason other than Equal Opportunity purposes or exercising a legal right or obligation required by law. Sensitive data includes your racial or ethnic origin, sexual life, political beliefs, trade union membership, religious beliefs, physical or mental health and criminal offences. If you have particular enquiries about Data Protection you are welcome to contact us, e-mail: jobs@aston.ac.uk Website Terms of Use Aston University reserves the right to change the website terms of use. You are responsible for regularly reviewing these terms of use. Your continued use of the Aston University jobs website constitutes your agreement to all such terms and conditions. The service is offered free to applicants of Aston University and may be terminated at any time, although there is no intention to withdraw the service. The Aston University jobs website and Aston University cannot be held responsible for any loss or damage due to the failure or termination of the service, although we will make reasonable efforts to let you know in advance of foreseeable service interruptions. Confirmation of registration will be sent by the Human Resources (HR) Office to the e-mail address you supply on registering. The service is strictly for personal and non-commercial use. It is not intended as a business service (e.g. a helpdesk or ordering e-mail address) and the HR Office reserves the right to terminate the service if business use is evident. While the HR Office and the University will not make any attempt to gain access to the content of e-mails, their complete security cannot be guaranteed since e-mail is not a secure transmission medium. You undertake to register for the Aston University jobs website using accurate and current information about yourself, including your correct name, address and any other requested information. If you see anything on the Aston University jobs website which appears to infringe this Agreement, then please contact us by emailing jobs@aston.ac.uk . If any third party site is linked to/from the Aston University jobs website, it does not mean that Aston University endorses, or has any responsibility for the site in question, or anything which appears on it. Your use of the Aston University jobs website is entirely at your own risk. When registering with the website, either to make an application or to receive job alerts, we will hold your information securely on the system. If you do not login to your account for a period of 12 months your account will be automatically deleted. We will contact you 1 month before your account is deleted to warn you. If you would like to request your account is deleted before this time please contact us by e-mailing hrsystems@aston.ac.uk . Cookies Cookies are used on this website to allow access to authenticated areas of the website (e.g. applying for a vacancy), for storing individual user preferences, and for gathering analytical visitor data.  For more information please visit the Cookies information page . Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
