    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1305-26": {
      "title": "Social Media Co-ordinator",
      "description": "1305-26 Social Media Co-ordinator - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Social Media Co-ordinator Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £27,319 to £29,588\n            per annum Grade: Grade 06 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Friday 18 September 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 01 October 2026 Reference: 1305-26 Release Date: Thursday 27 August 2026 Are you passionate about content creation and mastering social media algorithms? Aston University is seeking a creative and organised Social Media Coordinator to help deliver our social media strategy. Working within the Digital Content and Experiences team. You will plan, create and schedule content across our five main channels: Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, X and Facebook, with the possibility of supporting new social media platforms should they be relevant for the audiences of the university. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who loves making short form video content, social media graphics and capturing photography, who wants to see their content reach a real audience. You will brief and collaborate with our team of Student Content Creators, support the activity of colleagues across the university via promotion and help shape Aston’s digital footprint in the ever-evolving world of social media.  You will also respond to our online communities, acting as a point of customer service for the university and report on channel performance at regular intervals. As the successful candidate, you should have experience of delivering digital marketing activity for a company or organisation, or a portfolio of work, created alongside a degree or working as an independent content creator. Some experience of social media Scheduling and Monitoring tools such as Iconosquare, Orlo or Hootsuite would be useful. Additionally, it would be desirable for the successful candidate to have strong written English and proofreading skills alongside confidence in, or a willingness to learn applications such as Photoshop, Adobe Express, Canva, Premiere Pro or CapCut. Outside of this, all roles in the marketing team are expected to support during our biggest moments of the year, including Graduation, A Level Results Day and Open Days which may involve very infrequent weekend work, 1-2 weekends a year. This role is subject to a satisfactory standard DBS check. What\nwe offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 25 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa . Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1098-26": {
      "title": "Outreach Assistant",
      "description": "1098-26 Outreach Assistant - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Outreach Assistant Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £27,319 to £29,588\n            per annum Grade: Grade 06 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Monday 07 September 2026 Interview Date: Monday 28 September 2026 Reference: 1098-26 Release Date: Wednesday 19 August 2026 Are you passionate about helping young people explore their future opportunities? Aston University is seeking an enthusiastic and organised Outreach Assistant to support the delivery of our student recruitment and outreach activities. Working within the Student Recruitment and Outreach team, you will help deliver our Outreach programmes by coordinating events, deliver presentations, and represent Aston University at schools, colleges, UCAS fairs and on-campus events. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who enjoys working with young people, organising events and building relationships with a wide range of stakeholders. You'll have the chance to make a real difference by supporting students on their journey to higher education As the successful candidate, you will be educated to degree level (or equivalent) and have experience of working with young people, delivering presentations and providing excellent customer service. Strong communication, organisation and IT skills are essential, along with an understanding of the UK education system. Experience within higher education, event planning or widening participation activities would be advantageous.  The role requires occasional evening and weekend working, travel across the UK and a full UK driving licence. This role is subject to satisfactory enhanced DBS check. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 25 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
