    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=0965-26": {
      "title": "H & S Business Partner, Radiation Lead",
      "description": "0965-26 H & S Business Partner, Radiation Lead - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies H & S Business Partner, Radiation Lead Health, Safety & Business Continuity Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £38,784 to £46,049\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Part Time\n            (0.8) Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Friday 11 September 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 13 October 2026 Reference: 0965-26 Release Date: Friday 21 August 2026 Aston University are looking to recruit for an exciting opportunity within a forward-thinking Health & Safety Team. As a H&S Business Partner, you will work with colleagues within your designated schools and departments to provide professional advice and assistance to ensure legal compliance and to incorporate best practice into all aspects of their operations. You will support the Head of H&S to deliver the objectives in the University’s H&S Strategy and drive the continuous improvement of H&S Management throughout the university. You will work closely with the H&S Responsible Person designated schools and departments to deliver a high quality service. The role is advertised at 0.8 FTE - with the expectation being 4 days per week. Duties include: Support H&S best practice and compliance through coaching, mentoring and the identification, development and delivery of training to facilitate this; Support the monitoring of risk assessment completion and quality of local arrangements across the ECD; Coordinating health surveillance requirements have been adequately identified and where necessary referrals for tests are taken and recorded; Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to ensure compliance with H&S legislation; Attending the relevant H&S Committese and provide technical H&S advice; Coordinate the development and maintenance of local systems and processes which enable active and reactive monitoring to take place such as inspection and audit; Assisting with investigating accidents and incidents to determine their causes and make appropriate recommendations for improvements and preventative measures; Undertaking training as required across all job disciplines in the H&S Unit to ensure continued customer service during absences The ideal candidate will have: Level 6 Qualification in Occupational Health & Safety Management or a willingness to work towards Experience of managing or advising on H&S an educational environmental Membership of IOSH or equivalent professional body Good current knowledge of H&S legislation and regulations related to estates What we offer: Aston University is a vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Hybrid working is possible for this role, which means working both on campus and from home depending on the activity. Further information on hybrid working can be found here . Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days of bank holiday and University closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family-friendly policies. On-site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available. Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Previous applicants need not apply. Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 22nd July 2025.  If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting.See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1221-26": {
      "title": "Marketing and Communications Officer",
      "description": "1221-26 Marketing and Communications Officer - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Marketing and Communications Officer Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £31,236 to £36,636\n            per annum Grade: Grade 07 Contract Type: Fixed Term\n              \n                (9 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Friday 18 September 2026 Interview Date: Friday 02 October 2026 Reference: 1221-26 Release Date: Thursday 27 August 2026 Aston University is looking for a creative and enthusiastic Marketing and Communications Officer to join the team on a fixed-term basis, at an exciting time for the university. Working in a fast-paced environment, you will support and enhance the delivery of internal communications for a community of more than 3,000 staff and 17,000 students, creating clear, effective communications, campaigns and projects, with a particular focus on the One Aston intranet and student portal. Working closely with the Student and Internal Communications Managers, you will use CRM and CMS systems such as Dynamics 365, Mailchimp and Sharepoint to develop content for a range of digital channels including emails, newsletters and intranet pages. You will support communication campaigns for university initiatives and events, and use your data analytical experience to assist in monitoring and reporting on the effectiveness of communication activities. You will play an important role in delivering communications that support strategic goals, change management and engagement. You will also support crisis or urgent communications when required. We are looking for someone with proven experience in managing communications across multiple digital channels with a number of stakeholders, and a talent for creating and editing content for diverse audiences. Strong written and verbal communication skills, a keen eye for detail, the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and a collaborative approach to working across departments are all essential for success in this role. Experience of working in higher education would be advantageous too. This role is subject to satisfactory basic DBS check. For further information about this position, please contact Peter Kiddle, Internal Communications Manager, at p.kiddle@aston.ac.uk. What\nwe offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. The role is offered as 'dynamic working', which means working both on campus and from home dependent on the activity. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor the successful candidate if they are eligible for one of the salary discount options. Please see here for details about when you can be paid less for a Skilled Worker visa: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa/when-you-can-be-paid-less Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
