    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1269-26": {
      "title": "Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec)",
      "description": "1269-26 Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £58,225 to £67,468\n            per annum Grade: Grade 10 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Monday 21 September 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 07 October 2026 Reference: 1269-26 Release Date: Wednesday 02 September 2026 We are looking for a dynamic and commercially focused Deputy Director (Marketing & Student Recruitment) , with extensive experience in delivering HE marketing, to lead our student marketing and recruitment activity and deliver our ambitious student recruitment targets. With responsibility for generating an annual student recruitment income target of over £80m, you will develop and implement an insight-led, omni-channel marketing and recruitment strategy spanning domestic and international markets. You will lead teams covering market research, UK recruitment and outreach, paid media and campaigns, international and omnichannel marketing, CRM and conversion. This is a high-profile leadership role, working closely with senior colleagues across our university to deliver an excellent prospect and applicant journey and maximise applications, conversion and enrolments across multiple markets, whilst successfully communicating the Aston brand. You will champion a data-driven, customer-first culture, using market insight, innovation and digital marketing to drive applications, enrolments and return on investment. You will have a track record of improving lead generation, conversion, processes and customer journeys within a large university setting. Experience in developing high performing teams is essential, and you will be someone who thrives under pressure, with the ability to articulate a clear vision and motivate others to achieve it. We are seeking an experienced senior marketing leader with a strong track record of leading large, multi-disciplinary teams, delivering student recruitment growth and achieving financial targets. You will bring substantial expertise across the marketing mix, including CRM, advertising, brand, market research and digital marketing, alongside the ability to influence senior stakeholders and build high-performing teams. This role is subject to a satisfactory Enhanced DBS check. What\nwe offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 04 April 2024. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Reader in Aerospace Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
