    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1223-26": {
      "title": "Student Life Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "1223-26 Student Life Operations Coordinator - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Student Life Operations Coordinator Chief Student Officer Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £31,236 to £36,636\n            per annum Grade: Grade 07 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours BST on Sunday 06 September 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 22 September 2026 Reference: 1223-26 Release Date: Monday 17 August 2026 Aston University’s 2030 strategy is Inclusive, Entrepreneurial and Transformational. We are building a new model of university for a changing world, delivering measurable impact for our students, staff, partners and communities. Within this vision, the Student Life Directorate plays a central role in assisting students from transition through to successful completion, providing expert guidance on engagement, wellbeing and student success. The role holder will provide centralised operational, project, governance, systems, finance and compliance coordination across Student Life. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who is highly organised, calm under pressure, confident with digital systems and motivated by improving how services work behind the scenes. Key Responsibilities and Priorities: Directorate-wide operational coordination Meeting, governance and action tracking Digital process improvement using Microsoft 365 tools Student Life finance processing through Unit4 ERP/Agresso, departmental purchasing and budget reconciliation Compliance, audit, risk, health and safety and reporting support Cross-team collaboration and high-quality records management About You: You are an excellent organiser who can bring structure to complexity. You are comfortable using digital tools and interested in improving processes rather than simply maintaining them. You can manage sensitive information, deadlines and competing priorities with discretion and accuracy. You are confident working across multiple teams and following up actions professionally. You will have a degree-level qualification or equivalent relevant professional experience, with experience of operational, administrative, project, governance, compliance, health and safety or finance coordination in a complex organisation. Experience in Higher Education or student-facing professional services would be advantageous. Experience supporting operational processes such as health and safety, project coordination or compliance monitoring would also be helpful You are comfortable using using Microsoft 365 tools such as Lists, SharePoint, Power BI or Power Automate. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 22 July 2025. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled